<title>SINGAPORE: Hup Seng Huat after-tax profit up.</title>
<headline>Hup Seng Huat after-tax profit up.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Profit after tax		     6.24  vs   4.86</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		  10.00  vs  10.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    2.43  vs   1.93</p>
<p>    Turnover				66.44  vs  46.92</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.70  vs   1.09</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.13  vs   0.07</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     0.43  vs   0.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 8.73  vs   7.40</p>
<p>    Tax					2.49  vs   2.55</p>
<p>    Minorities  (gain)		   0.16  vs   0.02</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries  (gain)	    0.16  vs   nil</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:    January 27, 1997</p>
<p>Last day books open:  January 9, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Hup Seng Huat Co Ltd's principal activities are dealing in hardware and property investment. Profit after tax is before minorities and extraordinaries.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
